Important terms - Volume of distribution, Elimination half life

First order elimination rate constant, k = 0.692/(t1/2)

Distribution volume and weight determine Volume of distribution -> determines elimination rate based on half-life (CL = Vd* 0.693/t(1/2))
-> From infusion rate and elimination rate, determine steady state concentration (Css)

Some drugs take a long time to reach steady state levels, those need a loading dose.

Creatinine clearance = Urine volume *  Urine concentration /Plasma concentration

C (ss) = Rate of creatinine synthesis / C (cl), for drug infusion/intermittent dosing, C (ss) = %F*Dose/(Dosing interval*C(Cl))

